  "source_hints": null,
  "history": null,
  "answer": "The RFP scores qualifying proposals on a **100-point scale**:\n\n| Evaluation criterion | Points |\n|---|---:|\n| Vendor history and depth of public defined-contribution plan experience | 10 |\n| Scope of vendor operations and ability to provide the full range of requested services | 20 |\n| Plan sponsor experience, including website access, administration and compliance, relationship management, reporting, and industry/trend communication | 30 |\n| Participant communication and education, including website and call-center services, issue resolution, customized materials, onsite representatives, and guidance tools | 30 |\n| Overall cost to the plans and participants | 10 |\n| **Total** | **100** |\n\nProposals are first screened for timeliness and compliance with minimum qualifications and other requirements. The RFP notes that neither the lowest-priced nor the highest-scoring proposal is necessarily selected. Source: *Delaware Office of the State Treasurer, 2021 RFP*, Section VI.B, pp. 19–20.",
